        "role": "user",
        "content": "{\"initial_observation\":{\"company\":\"CLOSE_fin_02\",\"message\":\"The ledger is accessed through the supplied SQL tools.\"},\"max_actions\":10,\"task\":\"Company CLOSE_fin_02 keeps a single heterogeneous ledger table. Every record type is stored in ledger, so SQL self-joins and CTEs can be used. Close the payable ledger as it was known at recorded_at <= 2026-10-24T12:00:00, for business_date <= 2026-10-23. All timestamps are UTC ISO text. Start by excluding rows with future business dates and rows recorded late, then keep only the highest revision for each (kind,event_key). If that latest row has status void, the key is removed entirely; never fall back to an older row. Invoice rows use event_key as the invoice ID; payment, credit and hold rows use invoice_id to point to their parent invoice. Keep the active invoices for vendor BLUE with due_date <= 2026-10-30. Payments and credits reduce the gross amount_minor, in the invoice currency. Active holds reduce the remaining amount; holds with status release or void do not. Clamp as follows: remaining=max(0,gross-sum(payments)-sum(credits)), then unheld=max(0,remaining-sum(active holds)). For each invoice, pick the active terms row that has the same terms_code and the greatest business_date <= the invoice business_date (applying the same revision and as-of filtering). The discounted amount is unheld * (10000-discount_bps)/10000 only when 2026-10-23 <= discount_until; otherwise it is unheld. Next, pick the active FX row for that invoice's currency with the greatest business_date <= the invoice business_date. Convert to USD cents using fx_num/fx_den. Round only this final per-invoice amount to the nearest cent, rounding exact halves up. Sum the rounded per-invoice USD cents. Invoices in USD also have FX rows. Do not net invoices together before rounding. Submit only the integer number of USD cents.\",\"task_id\":\"fin-02\",\"tools\":[{\"description\":\"Get a list of available table names for a company.\",\"name\":\"get_descriptions\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"company_name\":{\"description\":\"The name of the company\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"company_name\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"description\":\"Get table metadata: description, columns, types, unique values.\",\"name\":\"get_table_info\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"company_name\":{\"description\":\"The name of the company\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"table_name\":{\"description\":\"The name of the table\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"company_name\",\"table_name\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"description\":\"Execute a SQL query on a table. Select * not allowed.\\n\\nFilters are required: WHERE, HAVING, IN, NOT IN, EXISTS, NOT EXISTS,\\nANY, SOME, ALL, LIKE, NOT LIKE, BETWEEN, NOT BETWEEN, IS NULL,\\nIS NOT NULL, CASE, FILTER.\",\"name\":\"sql_query\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"company_name\":{\"description\":\"The name of the company\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"query\":{\"description\":\"SQL query to execute (must include filters)\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"table_name\":{\"description\":\"The name of the table\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"company_name\",\"table_name\",\"query\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"description\":\"Submit a final answer for the question.\",\"name\":\"submit_answer\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"answer\":{\"description\":\"The final answer to submit\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"answer\"],\"type\":\"object\"}}]}"
